# =============================================================================
# gitleaks allowlist — deliberately suppressed findings
# =============================================================================
# Entries are FINGERPRINTS (commit:file:rule:line), not paths, so suppression
# is pinned to the exact historical blob. A later real secret in the same file
# produces a different fingerprint and is still reported. Never add a bare path
# here — that would blind the scanner to the whole file.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# `gitleaks detect` scans history and reported six findings, all of them fake
# tokens in artifice-transcribe's token-redaction tests. Those tests exist
# precisely to prove that a token is redacted before it reaches a log, the job
# history, or /health/detailed — so they must contain something token-shaped.
# The values are obviously synthetic:
#
#   hf_abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz123456   the alphabet
#   hf_aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa              repeated 'a'
#   sk-bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb              repeated 'b'
#   hf_real-secret-token-12345            a placeholder that says so
#
# A scan that always reports six findings trains people to skip reading it,
# which is how a real leak gets waved through. Six expected findings is not a
# baseline; it is noise that defeats the gate.
#
# BEFORE ADDING TO THIS FILE
#
# Read the matched value in the source first and confirm it is synthetic. If a
# finding cannot be shown to be fake, it is not a false positive — rotate the
# credential and rewrite the history instead of listing it here.
#
# RELATED, AND NOT FIXED BY THIS FILE
#
# CI's gitleaks step passes for an unrelated reason: actions/checkout@v7 makes a
# shallow clone, so `gitleaks detect` scans one commit rather than the branch's
# history, and would not catch a secret introduced in an earlier commit of a PR.
# Setting `fetch-depth: 0` on that job makes the gate real — and needs this file
# in place first, or the six fixtures below would turn it permanently red.
# =============================================================================

